In a BST, LCA is the first node where p and q diverge (one on each side).

```python
def lowest_common_ancestor(root, p, q):
    while root:
        if p.val < root.val and q.val < root.val:
            root = root.left
        elif p.val > root.val and q.val > root.val:
            root = root.right
        else:
            return root
```

